ttyctl - control console input

SYNOPSIS
    int ttyctl(int fd, int request);

DESCRIPTION
    The requests below are declared in tty.h. TTY_ISATTY checks that fd
    refers to the system console. A mode change requires a readable console
    descriptor.

    TTY_CBREAK gives the calling foreground process immediate, unechoed
    input. Read returns available bytes without waiting for a newline.
    Keyboard navigation keys are encoded as escape sequences. Terminal
    interrupt, quit, suspend and flow control keys still act on the console.

    TTY_CANON releases the caller's cbreak mode. Mode ownership is suspended
    when another job takes the foreground. The kernel releases it on exit or
    successful exec. A forked child starts in canonical mode.

RETURN VALUES
    ttyctl returns 0 on success or -1 on error.

SEE ALSO
    man(1), sh(1), execve(2)
